id: pm-brief-03r3
title: Renew only affected handoff obligations after source revisions change
description: "Receiver-specific repair deltas over immutable acknowledged handoff contracts, using native tracker comments without another store."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: handoff,repair-deltas
created_at: "2026-10-25T05:19:04.353Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T11:28:07.537Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T11:28:07.529Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T08:08:28.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: One changed dependency in a 50-item packet yields one affected-obligation group; unchanged acknowledgments remain valid; renewal against an old target revision is refused; typed SDK and CLI expose compact bounded TOON/JSON and remedies; seeded state model covers at least 500 sequences and competing transitions at every step; non-git public tracker validation and npm/Bun CI release gates pass.
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T05:19:15.879Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against the pinned CLI SDK, pm-context freshness and handoff generation, pm-review and pm-ops, and existing handoff.ts. Native comments own durable receipts and atomic ifAbsent append; listAllComplete plus certifyCompleteListResult own source completeness. Existing show marks the entire packet stale, and context-freshness validates source manifests; neither computes receiver-specific obligation repair. Implement repair/renew on the existing immutable Decision contract, grouping each focus and uncovered evidence root by its transitive blocker closure; shared questions/assumptions apply conservatively to each focus group. No new handoff store or import/sync engine."
  "2026-10-25T05:25:03.667Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed inspectHandoffRepair/renewHandoff and repair/renew CLI commands. Group targets bind the immutable contract to complete native source rows, including update coordinates. Native token-owned lease spans planning through verification; native ifAbsent append owns durable receipt idempotency; foreign receipt-shaped comments are skipped with indexed reasons. The 50-row acceptance scenario passes: one changed dependency yields one group and 24 unchanged acknowledgments. Seeded 500-sequence SDK readback test and every-boundary interleaving tests are running; local typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass."
  "2026-10-25T05:29:00.698Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing group-level preservation in repairSnapshot with legacy whole-packet invalidation makes the 50-row acceptance test fail (25 groups instead of 1). Restored the implementation afterward. Public main snapshot 6f93af2 measured 95 source items with zero source writes; a separate disposable derived tracker seeds 3 groups and one edit, then read-only measurement yields 1 affected group, 2 preserved acknowledgments, 694 delta JSON bytes versus 1040 packet bytes, 530 conservative tokens and 99 ms; renewal yields 3 valid acknowledgments. Seeded model exposed native no-op operations; the reference now explicitly permits unchanged SDK state rather than requiring a write for every input."
  "2026-10-25T05:32:38.195Z",codex-agent,"Local validation passed: 500 seeded sequences (seed 0x5eed2025), 499 older-input replays, 452 changed-revision round trips, 48 native no-op sequences. SDK readback preserves contracts, whitespace/CRLF responses, relationships and native source fields. pm test --run --only-last --progress passed 24 targeted tests; 2 final race regressions passed after strengthening exact-target verification. The 18 interleavings verify all six source-read/append/verification boundaries for source edits, identical native peer appends and foreign comments, including lease ownership through verification. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and diff whitespace checks pass. Full npm/Bun release checks are delegated to unchanged CI release-gate jobs; no local full gate on the saturated host."
  "2026-10-25T05:33:55.264Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted pm test run passes 25 tests with zero failures/skips, including the newer-peer revision race and native field/whitespace readback assertions. CI-identity isolated-home pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passes. The ordinary host health read encounters an existing global pm-github host-version skew (pinned SDK 2026.10.20 versus global extension host 2026.10.24); no dependency or global configuration changed. Repo-pinned SDK stays unchanged as required. The item is released, remains in_progress for orchestrator verification, and the PR will carry exact-head npm/Bun gate evidence."
  "2026-10-25T05:40:14.015Z",codex-agent,"Initial CI run 40166023258 exercised all 599 tests and the 500-sequence model. It exposed two missed integration expectations: command registration and renderer-ownership tests still listed only the previous command set, so the renderer test exited before its coverage assertions. Updated both expected command lists, asserted repair/renew flags and explicitly checked that native structured repair/renew output is not intercepted by the document renderer. Thresholds remain unchanged; rerunning targeted integration checks, then CI on the correction."
  "2026-10-25T05:40:38.158Z",codex-agent,"Integration correction verified: the two command-registration/renderer tests now pass through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Production code and coverage thresholds are unchanged; this restores the renderer coverage that the outdated command list prevented. Releasing for the next exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-25T05:43:52.900Z",codex-agent,"DeepScan exposed one unused test import (readFile); removed it. This is a static-only correction, with no behavior or threshold change. The final pushed head will rerun the full npm/Bun release gates; earlier in-flight heads are not final acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-25T07:29:25.732Z",codex-agent,"Read-only review blocked PR 179: removing A blocked-by B then renewing A pruned still-required evidence on B from the target. Reusing this item, with a clean worktree at 39ace44. Close the class by storing SDK-read dependency sets (item revisions, edges and evidence links) on initial acknowledgments and renewals, comparing each recorded set plus newly required dependencies without pruning prior coverage. Add the exact reported regression and a seeded 500-sequence graph/evidence model with acknowledgment, renewal, graph/link edits, item edits and deletion; record a behavioral revert proof and rerun final-head CI."
  "2026-10-25T07:43:16.227Z",codex-agent,"Recorded coverage implementation and fixed regression pass for docs/files/tests: after removing A-to-B and renewing A, B link removal, edits and deletion still invalidate A. Coverage stores item snapshots plus native edge/link coordinates and full-metadata hashes, and refreshes retained identities plus new dependencies from certified SDK reads. A transitive non-evidence regression and legacy/foreign-inventory cases extend the class proof. Targeted handoff tests currently pass 27 checks with 100 percent line/function coverage; new seeded graph/evidence model is running 500 independent sequences with seeds 0xdecafbad and 0x1052026."
  "2026-10-25T07:44:10.701Z",codex-agent,"Recorded-dependency revert proof: replaced dependencySet recorded-identity comparison with the former current-focus-closure projection, ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"recorded dependency regression\" test/handoff-coverage.test.ts, and observed the regression fail because the renewed snapshot omitted the evidence item after edge removal. Only that changed function was behaviorally reverted; the source was restored in finally. The restored implementation retains both covered items and their SDK-read native edge/link inventories."
  "2026-10-25T07:47:05.385Z",codex-agent,"Recorded-dependency state model passed 500 sequences using seeds 0xdecafbad and 0x1052026. Generated operation counts, including no-op attempts on absent targets: acknowledge 960, renew 887, add/remove blocker 473/223, add/remove evidence 455/348, evidence/focus edits 468/479, deletion 472. Every step compared pending groups, changed item ids, missing evidence and validity counts against independent maps of SDK-read recorded source state; stored item/edge/link sets were verified through SDK reads. Targeted pm test run passed 28 tests; typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Public read-only snapshot recheck remains 95 source items, zero source writes, one affected group, two preserved, 694 delta bytes versus 1040 packet bytes, 530 token ceiling; measured 30 ms. The recorded-dependency revert proof is documented above. Full release gates will rerun in CI on the pushed fix."
